hadiths[9]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18162","Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Salih, from Abu Abdur-Rahman al-Sulami who said: I heard Wabisah ibn Mabad, Companion of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to ask him about righteousness and sin, so he said: You have come to ask about righteousness and sin? I said: By Him who sent you with the truth, I came to you asking you about nothing else. So he said: Righteousness is what your chest is at ease with, and sin is what rankles in your chest, even if people give you a verdict about it."
"18163","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah who said: I heard Hilal ibn Yasaf narrating, from Amr ibn Rashid, from Wabisah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw a man pray alone behind the row, so he commanded him to repeat his prayer."
"18164","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Zubayr Abu Abdussalam, from Ayyub ibn Abdullah ibn Mikraz, from Wabisah ibn Mabad who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, intending to leave nothing of righteousness and sin but ask him about it, when there was a crowd with him. So I went stepping over the people, and they said: Away, O Wabisah, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, away, O Wabisah. I said: I am Wabisah, let me come near him, for he is among the most beloved of people to me to come near. So he said to me: Come near, O Wabisah, come near, O Wabisah. So I came near him until my knee touched his knee, and he said: O Wabisah, shall I tell you what you came to ask me about, or will you ask me? I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me. He said: You came to ask me about righteousness and sin. I said: Yes. So he gathered his three fingers and began tapping my chest with them, saying: O Wabisah, ask your own self; righteousness is what the heart is at rest with and the soul is at rest with, and sin is what rankles in the heart and wavers in the chest, even if people give you verdicts. Sufyan said: And give you verdicts."
"18165","Waki narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Husayn, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Ziyad ibn Abi al-Jaad who said: He set me before Wabisah ibn Mabad, who said: This narrated to me that a man prayed behind the row alone, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded him to repeat his prayer."
"18166","Waki narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Ziyad ibn Abi al-Jaad narrated to me, from his uncle Ubayd ibn Abi al-Jaad, from Ziyad ibn Abi al-Jaad, from Wabisah ibn Mabad, that a man prayed behind the rows alone, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded him to repeat."
"18167","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shimr ibn Atiyyah, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Wabisah ibn Mabad who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about a man who prayed behind the rows alone, so he said: He repeats the prayer."
"18168","Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us, from Shubah, Amr ibn Murrah narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Amr ibn Rashid, from Wabisah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw a man praying alone in the row, so he commanded him to repeat the prayer."
"18169","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, al-Zubayr Abu Abdussalam informed us, from Ayyub ibn Abdullah ibn Mikraz, and he did not hear it from him, he said: His companions narrated to me, and I saw him, from Wabisah al-Asadi. Affan narrated to me more than once and did not say his companions narrated to me. He said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, intending to leave nothing of righteousness and sin but ask him about it, with a group of Muslims around him asking him for verdicts. So I began stepping over them. They said: Away, O Wabisah, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. I said: Let me come near him, for he is the most beloved of people to me to come near. He said: Leave Wabisah, come near, O Wabisah, twice or thrice. He said: So I came near him until I sat before him, and he said: O Wabisah, shall I tell you or will you ask me? I said: No, rather tell me. So he said: You came to ask me about righteousness and sin. So he said: Yes. So he gathered his fingertips and began tapping my chest with them, saying: O Wabisah, ask your heart and ask your self, three times; righteousness is what the soul is at rest with, and sin is what rankles in the soul and wavers in the chest, even if people give you verdicts and give you verdicts."
"18170","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Husayn, from Hilal ibn Yasaf who said: Ziyad ibn Abi al-Jaad showed me an elder in al-Jazirah called Wabisah ibn Mabad. He said: So he set me before him and said: This narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw a man pray alone in the row, so he commanded him and he repeated the prayer. He said: And my father used to act by this hadith."
